# The demo walk: what the README's GIF is a recording of. It starts from the
# out/fx fixture — a set, an empty project, and SINE440.WAV sitting in the
# set's AUDIO pool — and builds a playing pattern out of it:
#
#   the firmware's splash — the Elektron mark assembling out of particles —
#     and then its LOADING FILES screen
#   assign SINE440 to track 1's STATIC machine, slot 1
#   back to the SRC page, PTCH / STRT / LEN / RATE visible
#   record mode, trigs on steps 1, 5, 9 and 13
#   PTCH up an octave and RATE down to its floor
#   PLAY (record mode stays on — the hardware does not care), then the
#   crossfader from B to A across two bars
#
# Record it with:
#   tests/build-fixture.sh
#   make demo-gif
#
# ☠ Waits are in GUEST time (wait_guest_ms), not wall time. The emulator does
# not hold realtime on a busy host — measured at load average 121, 52 s of
# wall-clock waits gave the guest 5.0 s of audio and every gesture landed in
# an Octatrack that had barely booted.
#
# ☠ Nothing here is saved. The walk ends on STOP and the run exits, so the
# fixture it was given is the fixture it leaves: run it twice and get the same
# recording. Do not add the PROJ save from fixture-trig.jsonl.
#
# ☠ The film starts at the first frame, deliberately: the splash is an
# ANIMATION of the Elektron mark assembling out of particles, it is running
# by 0.3 s, and it carries no text for a wait_text to gate on. Anything that
# waits before opening the recording misses it.
{"wait_text":"PTCH","timeout_ms":180000}
# ☠ Not a settle: the firmware is still reading the set off the card behind
# that dialog, and driving the panel before it closes loses keys. Waiting for
# it to GO is the observable the four-second guess used to stand in for.
{"wait_gone":"L0ADING FILE5","timeout_ms":60000}
# ☠ Do not cut this one down. The dialog closing is not the same as the
# firmware being ready for a chord: with 500 ms here, the FUNC+SRC tap below
# timed out on roughly one run in three, and it can never recover — FUNC is
# still held while the tap retries, so every retry is the same held-key chord
# the machine already ignored. MEASURED at 1500 ms: no failures.
{"wait_guest_ms":1500}
# The crossfader starts where the panel MCU parks it, at B. Say so anyway:
# the recording should not depend on that default.
{"crossfader":0}
{"wait_guest_ms":300}
# FUNC+SRC opens the machine setup for track 1, where the sample slot lives.
{"press":"FUNC"}
{"wait_guest_ms":250}
{"tap":"SRC","until":"5RC 5ETUP","verify_ms":20000,"timeout_ms":150000}
{"wait_guest_ms":200}
{"release":"FUNC"}
{"wait_guest_ms":350}
# Two pages right is the slot list; YES loads the first file in the pool.
{"tap":"RIGHT"}
{"wait_guest_ms":300}
{"tap":"RIGHT","until":"L0AD FILE T0 5TATIC 1","settle_ms":120,"verify_ms":20000,"timeout_ms":150000}
{"wait_guest_ms":300}
# ☠ The two until_gone taps below keep the full settle. Judging them early
# can read the screen before the dialog has opened and call that "gone".
{"tap":"YES","until_gone":"L0AD FILE T0 5TATIC 1","verify_ms":10000,"timeout_ms":180000}
{"wait_guest_ms":600}
{"mark":"assigned"}
# NO leaves setup: the SRC page comes back, PTCH / STRT / LEN / RATE and all.
{"tap":"NO","until_gone":"5RC 5ETUP","verify_ms":10000,"timeout_ms":120000}
{"wait_text":"PTCH","timeout_ms":60000}
{"wait_guest_ms":400}
# Grid recording: REC lights, and a trig key toggles that step.
#
# ☠ The lamp numbers are BIT ids, not lamp ids — every lamp owns two, so trig
# N's "a trig lives here" bit is 2*(N-1): 0, 8, 16, 24 for steps 1, 5, 9, 13.
# Gating each tap on its own bit is what lets these run at a player's pace:
# the step ends when the LED says the trig landed, not after a fixed settle,
# and a lost key is retried instead of silently missing from the pattern.
# settle_ms trims the pause before that judging starts, which is safe here
# because the condition is positive — an early poll just polls again.
{"tap":"REC"}
{"wait_guest_ms":300}
{"tap":"TRIG1","until_lamp":0,"lit":1,"settle_ms":120,"verify_ms":8000}
{"tap":"TRIG5","until_lamp":8,"lit":1,"settle_ms":120,"verify_ms":8000}
{"tap":"TRIG9","until_lamp":16,"lit":1,"settle_ms":120,"verify_ms":8000}
{"tap":"TRIG13","until_lamp":24,"lit":1,"settle_ms":120,"verify_ms":8000}
{"mark":"trigs-placed"}
{"wait_guest_ms":400}
# ☠ The encoder index is the KNOB, not the parameter's place on the screen:
# knob-a..f are 0..5 and knob-level is 6, so on the playback page PTCH is
# knob A (0) and RATE is knob D (3). LEV belongs to the Level knob, which is
# why the screen's first column is not encoder 0.
#
# MEASURED, because neither parameter moves one unit per detent and neither
# cares how fast you turn (12 detents read the same at 117 ms, 33 ms and
# 12 ms apart, so nothing is lost at speed and no acceleration is applied):
#
#   PTCH  1/6 of a semitone a detent — 12 detents is +2.0, so an octave up
#         is 72 of them
#   RATE  one unit a detent, starting at +65 and stopping at -64 — 129 to
#         reach the floor, and a few more cost nothing once it is there
#
# The turn hint saturates after twelve detents either way, so both of these
# spend most of their length in its rotating state.
#
# Both hands at once: the first turn carries its own condition — a wait of no
# time at all — so the walk starts it and moves straight on to the second,
# which does the waiting for both. They are given the same length so they
# finish together.
{"encoder":0,"delta":1,"times":72,"over_ms":2600,"wait_guest_ms":0}
{"encoder":3,"delta":-1,"times":132,"over_ms":2600}
{"wait_guest_ms":500}
{"mark":"knobs"}
# Bit 1 is trig 1's other channel: the playhead crossing step 1. That is the
# evidence the transport actually started. Record mode stays on.
#
# The slide is hung on the PLAY tap so it leaves with the key rather than a
# beat later, once the tap has finished proving itself. One bar is four beats
# at the project's 120 BPM, so 4000 ms of guest time is the two bars asked
# for, and the wait below covers the slide plus the tap's own settle.
{"tap":"PLAY","crossfader":255,"over_ms":4000,"until_lamp":1,"lit":1,"settle_ms":120,"verify_ms":5000,"timeout_ms":120000}
{"mark":"playing"}
{"wait_guest_ms":3700}
{"mark":"faded"}
{"wait_guest_ms":800}
{"tap":"STOP"}
{"wait_guest_ms":900}
{"mark":"done"}
